{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>From the glow</b> — Its meaning is obscure. The established rule of the majority is [to read it as] עביו עברו עברו." "<b>Hailstones and coals of fire</b> — It is like iron that burns, and also kills by wind. The meaning is fear and terror in the enemies' hearts when they hear the sound of thunder."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is extremely cryptic; the phrase עביו עברו עברו may be a phonetic or masoretic notation rather than meaningful words. Rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:33.483353644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}